Package: REGATTA
Type: Package
Title: Reconciling eDNA Geographic Assignments via Taxonomy Table Adjustment
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Eldridge", "Wisely", email = "eldridge.wisely@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Ella", "Crotty", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Summary-table format designed by Ella Crotty.")
    )
Author: Eldridge Wisely [aut, cre],
    Ella Crotty [ctb] (Summary-table format designed by Ella Crotty.)
Maintainer: Eldridge Wisely <eldridge.wisely@gmail.com>
Description: Reconcile eDNA metabarcoding taxonomic assignments against a
    regional species checklist, downgrading the taxonomic specificity of
    assignments to taxa with no records in the study area rather than
    discarding them. Such geographically spurious species-level calls arise
    from genetic and geographic gaps and outdated names in reference
    databases, not from the DNA itself. Works without manual curation and
    preserves as much taxonomic specificity as the regional evidence supports. The package optionally also
    reconciles two classifier outputs (e.g. against a global vs. a
    locally-curated reference database) using percent identity to pick
    the better-supported call and falling back to the lowest common
    ancestor when the two disagree.
